  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sierra Leone Threshold - Agriculture Project - Non-allocated Funds activity: Due Diligence funding is used to obtain sufficient information to evaluate, assess and appraise projects during program development, effectively oversee and monitor program implementation, conduct quality assurance, and then evaluate the results of the project once complete. In this particular project, due diligence funds were used to hire external technical assistance to support MCC&apos;s assessment and oversight of the MCA&apos;s agriculture projects to ensure country-led designs and subsequent implementation were consistent with MCC guidance.</narrative>
  </description>
